sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant User as User (browser/mobile)
    participant Auth as AuthController (iam)
    participant PG as PostgreSQL
    participant JWT as JwtService (iam)
    participant Filter as TenantContextFilter
    participant AuthZ as @PreAuthorize / AuthzGuard

    User->>Auth: POST /api/v1/auth/login {email, password}
    Auth->>PG: lookup User by email (tenant_id nullable for platform admins)
    PG-->>Auth: User row (BCrypt hash, role, tenant_id, site_ids)
    Auth->>Auth: BCrypt.matches(password, hash)
    Auth->>JWT: issue token(userId, email, role, tenant_id, site_ids[])
    JWT-->>Auth: signed JWT (HS256, 86400s expiry)
    Auth-->>User: 200 {token}

    Note over User: Client stores token (web: httpOnly cookie target,<br/>today: localStorage — see ADR-0601 migration note)

    User->>Filter: subsequent request, Authorization: Bearer JWT
    Filter->>Filter: verify signature + expiry
    Filter->>Filter: extract role, tenant_id, site_ids[]
    Filter->>Filter: set ThreadLocal TenantContext + RLS session var
    Filter->>AuthZ: proceed to controller method
    AuthZ->>AuthZ: check @PreAuthorize("hasRole('TENANT_ADMIN')")<br/>+ tenant_id matches resource?
    AuthZ-->>User: 200 (allowed) or 403 (role/tenant mismatch)

    Note over User,AuthZ: Edge/camera calls use a separate auth path:<br/>X-Gate-Key today, per-camera key/mTLS target — see ADR-0602.
